1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Welcome — today we build a complete retail data warehouse in Databricks for NovaMart.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:14,000
This open-source project takes you from raw files to analytics-ready Gold tables.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:22,000
We use medallion architecture: Bronze for raw, Silver for trusted, Gold for star schema.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Clone github.com/akhilvydyula01/databricks and open notebooks/data_warehouse.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,000
In Databricks Repos, add the Git folder, Pull latest, and attach a cluster.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Notebook 01 creates schema retail_dwh and sample customers, products, stores, and orders.

7
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Notebook 02 lands Bronze tables as-is, with lineage columns like ingested_at.

8
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Notebook 03 builds Silver: cast types, dedupe orders, and quarantine invalid amounts.

9
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Notebook 04 creates Gold dimensions and gold_fact_sales in a star schema.

10
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Notebook 05 demonstrates SCD Type 2 so customer city and segment history is preserved.

11
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Notebook 06 runs data quality gates before publishing analytics.

12
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Notebook 07 answers business questions: revenue by month, top products, store performance.

13
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Next, schedule it as a Databricks Job and try the student Returns assignment.

14
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Thanks for watching — like, subscribe, and build this in your own workspace.
